<node id="Agile Teams">
  <data key="d0">Agile Teams</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Agile Teams are cross-functional groups of professionals who collaborate to deliver iterative and incremental value using Agile methodologies. They operate within an Iteration or Program Increment and leverage frameworks such as Weighted Shortest Job First (WSJF) and Design Thinking to optimize their processes. By focusing on delivering incremental solutions, Agile Teams ensure continuous improvement and adaptability in their approach to achieving project goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Agile Teams are cross-functional groups that collaborate to deliver incremental value within an Iteration or Program Increment.&lt;SEP&gt;Agile Teams are groups of professionals who use Agile methodologies to deliver iterative and incremental solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-263dd2bc37bfae14dc8f9beff9e5d09e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df9cb7b8cf1803448d29a16d8b2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d07decf500a728985eee0f94204ebaf</data>
  <data key="d4">./data/US/User_Stories\agile terms and definitions.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1752851973</data>
</node>
