<node id="Prototype">
  <data key="d0">Prototype</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Prototype is the fourth stage of the Design Thinking process, involving the creation of low-fidelity models to explore and validate ideas.&lt;SEP&gt;Prototype is the fourth stage of the Design Thinking process, where low-fidelity models of solutions are created to explore and validate ideas.&lt;SEP&gt;Prototype is the fourth step in the Design Thinking process, involving the creation of low-fidelity models to explore and validate ideas, such as paper sketches, wireframes, or mockups.&lt;SEP&gt;Prototype is the fourth step in the Design Thinking process, involving the creation of low-fidelity models to explore and validate ideas, such as paper sketches, wireframes, or mockups.&lt;SEP&gt;Prototype is the fourth step in the Design Thinking process, involving the creation of low-fidelity models to explore and validate ideas, such as paper sketches, wireframes, or mockups.</data>
